# DHCP Configuration and Inter-Network Routing

This practical was performed using Cisco Packet Tracer to configure two separate LAN networks connected through two routers.

The practical demonstrates:

- DHCP configuration
- IPv4 addressing
- Router interface configuration
- Router-to-router WAN connectivity
- Static routing
- Default gateway configuration
- ARP
- ICMP
- Inter-LAN communication
- Packet simulation and hop-by-hop analysis

---

## 1. Network Topology

The topology consists of:

- 2 × Cisco 1841 Routers
- 2 × Cisco 2960-24TT Switches
- 6 × PCs
- Serial WAN connection between the routers
- wires copper straight-through
